{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $30$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-6{x}^{2} & =30 \\\\ \\frac{5{y}^{2}}{30}-\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{30} & =\\frac{30}{30} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfbe689c-ae04-5405-9a38-d80f10662a0b" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Equation of a Horizontal Hyperbola in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0891dd94-b53a-5be9-94e8-a0e0c9c1c704" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{18}-\\frac{y^2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291433} {:answer/id #uuid "d05d8e6b-b8a6-5d70-8c7d-652254c735d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{5}-\\frac{y^2}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d05d8e6b-b8a6-5d70-8c7d-652254c735d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{5}-\\frac{y^2}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291434} :answer-field/id #uuid "b79adcaf-6ade-55ae-aa66-51d0a8f1c324" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd3e8a9f-9cea-50dc-8383-28a926c25f80" :question/math-academy-id "q-320620" :question/problem "The equation of the hyperbola $18{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}=90$ in standard form is{{field-1}}\n$=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $90$ and then simplify, 