$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2} & =60 \\\\ \\frac{5{x}^{2}}{60}-\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{60} & =\\frac{60}{60} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{10} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfbe689c-ae04-5405-9a38-d80f10662a0b" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Equation of a Horizontal Hyperbola in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6525ed41-c128-5cab-ad4a-ac05a6ba9732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291447} {:answer/id #uuid "bbce63ae-d5ed-5f0d-84ac-95fa2f5fc126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291448} {:answer/id #uuid "40444dfd-c7bf-5a3d-bf41-02f7db7c814e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291449} {:answer/id #uuid "1e2d9b61-203c-5175-9472-a47831c8f720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291450} {:answer/id #uuid "b23b7406-f2d5-5e9b-99c4-e9468b43af9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b23b7406-f2d5-5e9b-99c4-e9468b43af9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291451} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4eb13d2-212a-5869-b456-2840166e6960" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4c6311a-6921-5ac2-942f-1759d226f36a" :question/math-academy-id "q-78234" :question/problem "Write the equation of the hyperbola $3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=18$ in standard form." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $18$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{18}-\\frac{2{y}^{2}}{18} & =\\frac{18}{18} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
